From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lavfi/rkrga: do not free a frame ff_filter_frame() has taken

Both async delivery sites free the output frame when delivery fails:

    filter_ret = r->filter_frame(outlink, aframe.dst->frame);
    if (filter_ret < 0) {
        av_frame_free(&aframe.dst->frame);

ff_filter_frame() owns the frame from the moment it is called. Its contract
says so -- "The receiving filter is responsible for unreferencing frame in
case of error" -- and its implementation does so on every negative return,
both the format-mismatch path and a ff_framequeue_add() failure. It frees
its own parameter, which leaves the caller's pointer dangling rather than
NULL, so av_frame_free() on it is a use-after-free followed by a second
free of the AVFrame allocation.

Drop the reference unconditionally, and account for it: the frame has left
the queue whether or not delivery succeeded, so `queued` must be
decremented on the error path too, which it previously was not.

r->filter_frame is always ff_filter_frame here -- vf_vpp_rkrga and
vf_overlay_rkrga both leave param.filter_frame NULL and ff_rkrga_init()
substitutes it -- so there is no override with different ownership rules.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavfilter/rkrga_common.c | 20 ++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavfilter/rkrga_common.c b/libavfilter/rkrga_common.c
index 8fe3a7c..1ca7d39 100644
--- a/libavfilter/rkrga_common.c
+++ b/libavfilter/rkrga_common.c
@@ -1340,13 +1340,13 @@ int ff_rkrga_filter_frame(RKRGAContext *r,
         set_rga_async_frame_lock_status(&aframe, 0);
 
         filter_ret = r->filter_frame(outlink, aframe.dst->frame);
-        if (filter_ret < 0) {
-            av_frame_free(&aframe.dst->frame);
-            return filter_ret;
-        }
+        /* ff_filter_frame() consumes the frame on every path, its error paths
+         * included, so drop our reference to it before looking at the result. */
+        aframe.dst->frame = NULL;
         aframe.dst->queued--;
+        if (filter_ret < 0)
+            return filter_ret;
         r->got_frame = 1;
-        aframe.dst->frame = NULL;
     }
 
     if (!picref_src)
@@ -1437,13 +1437,13 @@ int ff_rkrga_filter_frame(RKRGAContext *r,
         set_rga_async_frame_lock_status(&aframe, 0);
 
         filter_ret = r->filter_frame(outlink, aframe.dst->frame);
-        if (filter_ret < 0) {
-            av_frame_free(&aframe.dst->frame);
-            return filter_ret;
-        }
+        /* ff_filter_frame() consumes the frame on every path, its error paths
+         * included, so drop our reference to it before looking at the result. */
+        aframe.dst->frame = NULL;
         aframe.dst->queued--;
+        if (filter_ret < 0)
+            return filter_ret;
         r->got_frame = 1;
-        aframe.dst->frame = NULL;
     }
 
     return 0;
